==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hvíla|lang=non}}, akin to Gothic {{term|𐍈𐌴𐌹𐌻𐌰𐌽|sc=Goth|tr=ƕeilan||to pause, cease}}, from Gothic {{term|𐍈𐌴𐌹𐌻𐌰|sc=Goth|tr=ƕeila||hour}}, akin to Old High German {{term|hwila}} (or {{term|wila}} or {{term|hwil}}), a while (German {{term|Weile}}).

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f}}

# {{dated|lang=is}} a [[bed]]

===Verb===
'''hvíla''' ({{accusative}}) ([[hvíldi]], [[hvílt]])

# to [[rest]], especially resting or sleeping in a bed
#: ''Hér '''hvílir''' Jóhannes.''
#:: Here '''rests''' Johannes.
# to [[lie]], to [[sleep]]

